        "reasoning": "The Taylor-Green Vortex is a standard test case for validating numerical methods in fluid dynamics. The configuration requires a 2pi periodic cube with a grid size of 64^3 and 128^3 to assess convergence. The Reynolds number is set to 1600 with a viscosity of 1/1600. The simulation uses explicit diffusion only, without subgrid-scale models, Coriolis force, or buoyancy. The output includes volume-averaged kinetic energy E(t) and enstrophy Omega(t) every 0.1 time units from t=0 to t=20. Baseline weights: configuration_complexity=0.100, development_activity=0.100, domain_models=0.100, grid_specifications=0.200, path_hierarchy=0.150, physics_parameters=0.300, resource_requirements=0.050.",
